# Core role: Auto-generated ship catalog (macro → {class, hull, hardpoints, price, purchasable}).
# Generated by gamefiles/generate_data.py from X4 game files; re-run after updates.
#   class          — ship size class (ship_s, ship_m, ship_l, ship_xl, ship_xs)
#   max_hull       — base maximum hull HP before mods
#   price          — average buy price in credits (0 if the hull isn't sold)
#   hardpoints     — slot layout {type: {size: count}} from the hull component
#                    (type = weapon/turret/shield/engine; size = s/m/l/xl)
#   purchasable    — True if the player can buy this new at a shipyard. False
#                    for hulls only obtainable by capture or story reward (e.g.
#                    Xenon/Kha'ak ships) — still real, ownable ships.
#   flown          — False means no faction owns/flies this hull at all (NPC
#                    skin variant, escape pod, deployable drone, colony-ship
#                    set-piece part) — never a real or encounterable ship.
#                    The design builder's hull catalog drops these; naming
#                    tables (ships.py) keep them so any scanned entity still
#                    resolves to a name.
#   weapon_heat_factor — multiplies every mounted weapon's heat generation
#                    (1.0 = no effect, the common case). Confirmed against real
#                    tooltips: lowers Time to Overheat proportionally, does NOT
#                    affect Sustained Weapon Damage or Cooldown Duration.
#   ship_type      — the macro's own <ship type=...> role tag (e.g. 'destroyer',
#                    'heavyfighter', 'largeminer') — the game's own role
#                    classification, not guessed from the macro id.
#   purpose        — coarser <purpose primary=...> bucket: fight/trade/mine/
#                    build/auxiliary/salvage. '' if the macro has none.
#   makerrace      — <identification makerrace=...>, lowercase race key (e.g.
#                    'argon') — same key space as equipment's race field.
#   crew_capacity  — <people capacity=...>; None if the macro has no crew slot.
#   missile_storage/unit_storage — <storage missile=.. unit=..> counts; None if
#                    the macro has no such storage element.
#   cargo_max      — m3 capacity from the hull's cargo-bay macro (resolved via
#                    the ship macro's storage <connection>); None if the hull
#                    has no cargo bay (most fighters/drones).
#   cargo_tags     — ware-type tags on that cargo bay (e.g. 'container', 'solid',
#                    'liquid'); '' if cargo_max is None.
#   description/variation — flavour text + variant name (e.g. 'Vanguard'),
#                    resolved from the language file; '' if the macro has none.
